883c","position":"1788871759885160001-877fc06c-b8b2-441b-b0be-7f559e2328a3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"633c87617987b92391066e7e491feacea2f0c4b017a96f8bd4ebb771010d5427","event_uuid":"339035f7-7673-4d25-bfc2-d9c469f746c9","position":{"commit_sha":"ee938e6cd78fc57970dccdf946006451db9e3e11","position":"1788874628721445001-339035f7-7673-4d25-bfc2-d9c469f746c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8f6d11121e9c0b1aa913ae847d3932f46a1f7cfa36ead2cd87ca474426fad4ab","event_uuid":"d5491e72-3925-471b-a965-ce7c95aea6ef","position":{"commit_sha":"92908dc6de55325f2589d26e5eac190e93492306","position":"1788875298955004001-d5491e72-3925-471b-a965-ce7c95aea6ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b9ba9ff0898696f951eee662242ee56e877b3cb1ff421651196a562d08540525","event_uuid":"46f184be-773a-4f2f-af6d-88ebc137d32a","position":{"commit_sha":"c8437493230d42b4404af03a9ebab5c1c75f377d","position":"1788876919355495237-46f184be-773a-4f2f-af6d-88ebc137d32a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (complete; investigation only)\n\nOBSERVATION\nThe described perturbation removes both identity guards from a previously bound local/Jira pair: the binding-store entry and the Jira `rebar-id:<local_id>` label. The next pass creates one inbound local duplicate and one outbound Jira duplicate, then converges once the new entities are labelled/bound.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nTwo independent create arms fire in one reconcile pass. Inbound: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py:compute_binding_walk_mutations` considers every unbound snapshot key; `_adopt_stands_down` returns `False` when `_marked_local_ids(fields)` is empty, so the unlabelled original Jira issue is treated as Jira-native and emits an ADOPT create mutation. Outbound: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py:compute_outbound_mutations` chooses create solely when `binding_store.get_jira_key(local_id) is None`; `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py:create_one` dedups only with JQL `labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"`, which misses after label loss, then creates a new Jira issue and writes label/entity-property/binding.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nConfirmed with a bounded in-process harness using fake binding store/client and no production Jira. For an unbound local `loc-1` plus unbound Jira snapshot `DIG-1` with no labels, `compute_binding_walk_mutations` returned `adopted ['DIG-1']` and an inbound create mutation. The same pass's outbound differ returned a create mutation for `loc-1`; `create_one` searched exactly `labels = \"rebar-id:loc-1\"`, got no hits, created one Jira issue, added `rebar-id:loc-1`, set entity property `local_id=loc-1`, and `bind_confirm`ed it. This would have been disproven if either arm had used a third identity signal (for example Jira entity property) or if the outbound create branch considered more than binding+label.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nEither explicitly accept and pin the bounded +1/+1 behavior, or add a third durable identity check before outbound create/inbound adopt (most naturally reading the existing Jira `local_id` entity property) so simultaneous loss of binding+label still reconnects instead of duplicating.","timestamp":1788737395089398001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA/decision before implementation: the +1/+1 bounded duplicate is not acceptable as-is because it creates a durable extra rebar ticket and Jira issue that require manual disposition. The fix will add/use a third identity signal that survives loss of both the binding-store row and the rebar-id label: Jira entity property local_id, already written during Jira create writeback. Outbound create should consult that property before creating a replacement issue and reconnect when it matches; the perturbation test will pin no duplicate growth. This honors the package-move coordination note on gunshy-symmetric-barnacle by landing at the current src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler paths before the move carries it forward.","timestamp":1788869202069305001}],"created_at":1788641125855899001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4a794c67-5ffb-4cf9-9e5b-5f911059c921","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc"},{"link_uuid":"46f184be-773a-4f2f-af6d-88ebc137d32a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4699-656d-cab8-4870"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nMeasured, reproducible, and **bounded**: when a bound rebar<->Jira pair loses BOTH its binding-store entry and its `rebar-id:` label, the next reconcile pass creates **one extra rebar ticket and one extra Jira issue**, then converges. It is self-correcting — both new entities are bound and labelled in that same pass, so no further growth occurs — but the duplicate is real, durable, reaches Jira, and needs a human to disposition it.\n\nFound while experimentally excluding the reconciler as the producer of the 08-31/09-01 duplicate burst (`anarchic-princely-raven`, `00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc`). It is NOT that incident's cause — that was a local eval harness writing into the live store — but it is a genuine non-zero residual, filed separately so it is not buried inside a finding whose headline is \"excluded\".\n\n## Exact perturbation that produces it\n\nHarness: `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_echo_loop_experiment.py`, test `test_d_outbound_orphan_local_ticket_unbound_and_unlabelled` (real git + real ticket CLI + the stateful Jira fake; no production Jira or store).\n\n1. Start from a locally-authored rebar ticket, bound to its Jira issue, label present.\n2. Delete the binding-store entry AND remove the `rebar-id:<local_id>` label from the Jira issue — the create-then-crash / orphan shape (the applier died between materialising and `binding_store.save()`, which is deferred to end-of-pass at `persist_phase.py:140`).\n3. Run further passes.\n\n## Observed\n\n    local tickets: 2 -> 3   (+1)\n    jira issues  : 2 -> 3   (+1)\n    then stable — later passes issue ZERO writes\n\nTwo independent arms fire in the SAME pass:\n\n- **Inbound adopt** materialises an echo ticket from the now-unmarked issue: `_adopt_stands_down` (`binding_walk.py:375-411`) returns False for an unmarked key, so ADOPT proceeds and mints `jira-<key>`.\n- **Outbound create** mints a second Jira issue: `outbound_differ.py:588` keys create-vs-update solely off the binding store (now empty), and the dedup JQL at `dispatch_one.py:154` (`labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"`) MISSES with the label gone.\n\n## Why it converges\n\nBoth new entities are `bind_confirm`'d and labelled within that same pass, so the next pass takes the update branch at `outbound_differ.py:588` and the adopt arm skips the now-bound key at `binding_walk.py:202`. Growth is +1/+1 exactly once, not per-pass.\n\n## Why the existing guards do not prevent it\n\nEach guard alone is sufficient; this perturbation removes both. Measured in the same harness:\n\n- Label intact, binding gone (perturbation a): dedup JQL hits, **zero growth, zero Jira writes**.\n- Binding intact, label gone (perturbation b): outbound takes the update branch, **total no-op**.\n- Both gone (perturbation d): **+1/+1**.\n\n## Related but distinct\n\n- `injurious-neutral-glowworm` (`21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03`, CLOSED) — DC index lag. Its keyless-pending grace was verified WORKING in this harness: inside the grace window `is_keyless_pending_within_grace` (`dispatch_one.py:148-152`) defers the create and growth is zero. Past the grace one duplicate appears — the acknowledged boundary of a time-boxed grace, not a regression of that fix.\n- `nonmystic-topiary-toadfish` — the dedup JQL this perturbation defeats.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 Decision recorded: +1/+1 on simultaneous loss of both guards is NOT acceptable because it creates durable local and Jira duplicates requiring human disposition.\n- [ ] AC2 Add a third identity signal for the measured perturbation: enrich each fetched Jira snapshot entry by direct per-issue `get_issue_property(issue_key, \"local_id\")` reads, then use that property to suppress inbound adopt/snapshot-differ creates and outbound creates when it points at an active local ticket. This does not require knowing the key from the local id; the key comes from the ordinary fetched working-set issue.\n- [ ] AC3 Scope note: this fixes post-containment loss of binding+label where the already-written entity property remains. A crash before both label and property are written remains owned by the existing keyless-pending grace/recovery boundary.\n- [ ] AC4 A regression test pins no local/Jira duplicate growth for the perturbation above.\n\n## Priority rationale\n\np3. A single bounded, self-correcting duplicate per affected pair, requiring simultaneous loss of two independent guards. Not p2: it does not compound and does not grow across passes. Not p4: the duplicate is durable, reaches Jira, and needs manual disposition.\n## Implementation decision\n\nThe accepted branch is to fix, not accept, the +1/+1 duplicate. The third signal is not a reverse property lookup. The fetcher already has each Jira key in the working-set snapshot, so it can directly read that key's `local_id` entity property and attach it to the snapshot before the differs run. Outbound create then sees a Jira snapshot entry claiming the local id and re-confirms the binding instead of creating. The snapshot differ and binding-walk adopt arm also stand down for property-bound issues. This addresses the measured perturbation: a successfully contained Jira issue later loses its binding row and `rebar-id` label but retains the property. If a create crashes before the property write, the existing keyless-pending grace/recovery path remains the boundary.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"calls local_id property enrichment while staying under fetcher size target"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py","reason":"owns fetched snapshot local_id entity-property enrichment helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py","reason":"suppress outbound create and restore binding when property points at local ticket"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py","reason":"unbound adopt walk restores property-identified bindings instead of adopting"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"pure differ stands down when Jira local_id property points at an existing local id"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"snapshot-differ filter drops property-bound Jira-native emissions"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"apply property-bound snapshot-differ filter at legacy prev-vs-curr call site"},{"path":"tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_echo_loop_experiment.py","reason":"perturbation regression pins no +1/+1 growth"},{"path":"tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py","reason":"stateful fake supports issue property reads used by fetch enrichment"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4699-656d-cab8-4870"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e895e9d8-4235-4fed-9fac-6f860085e440","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f778-6dd7-8913-4043","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler creates one duplicate rebar ticket AND one duplicate Jira issue when a bound pair loses both its binding and its rebar-id label","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["25d570c6-aa61-4148-8a6c-7f8ccd7ee81d","96c7ae46-d695-4f0a-9193-c812388a207c","30673c2b-823d-4bf0-8012-0fba61cdaaca","fd23939e-e039-43a9-80e5-9aa7484a2ff4","e895e9d8-4235-4fed-9fac-6f860085e440","860d57b6-ddf3-498c-84a7-670eea772c2d","d4ace765-fa2f-4d4b-af2e-95dd262bd330","877fc06c-b8b2-441b-b0be-7f559e2328a3","339035f7-7673-4d25-bfc2-d9c469f746c9","d5491e72-3925-471b-a965-ce7c95aea6ef","46f184be-773a-4f2f-af6d-88ebc137d32a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788884995450400001,"uuid":"42c822e9-062d-4f54-ba7d-27f0cde3468b"}